# Review routing for this SDK.
#
# Beso owns it. Every SDK routes to him, and a PR carries exactly one reviewer --
# see brain PROCESS.md, "Exactly one reviewer per PR, and only Sid says when".
#
# One wildcard owner is the whole file. The eight per-path rules it replaces all
# resolved to a person anyway, and one of them -- /.github/workflows/ -- named
# two, so every CI change requested both reviewers, which is the thing the
# one-reviewer rule forbids.
#
# The file stays rather than being deleted, even though no other SDK has one.
# `main` sets require_code_owner_reviews, and a branch with that flag and no
# CODEOWNERS has no owners to require -- any single approval would clear a gate
# that is supposed to mean the SDK's owner looked at it.
#
# Provenance note, previously carried as its own rule: everything under
# /app/src/main/java/com/intempt/core/queue/ is the vendored delivery substrate
# from mixpanel-android. Review it as provenance -- confirm it matches upstream
# and that the Apache 2.0 change notices are intact -- rather than line by line.
